        <characteristic name="W" typeId="83ed-7b82-bf1f-e558">1</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="I" typeId="73b1-abe5-72f8-41e2">3</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="A" typeId="dddc-9fbd-b0fd-a480">1</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Ld" typeId="c435-6b14-f77e-3c72">7</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Galloper&apos;s Deployment" id="1fe3-5056-123a-ee2b" hidden="false" typeId="c1ac-c1c8-f9d5-9673" typeName="Special Rule">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9f84-4221-785a-db50">Guns may be deployed as single battery, or each of the gun teams might be deployed as separate teams, each gun operating as an independent unit. Bronzino may ride from one team to another, and any team he is with can test against his Leadership while he is in it.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Galloper&apos;s Function" id="8e85-a0d6-a610-768e" hidden="false" typeId="c1ac-c1c8-f9d5-9673" typeName="Special Rule">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9f84-4221-785a-db50">If the galloper gun is being charged by an enemy unit, the crew may hold or flee. If they flee, the gun is assumed to be attached and carried with the team with no movemet penalty. If the gun and crew are caught, they are destroyed. If they fight, they are considered to be in hand-to-hand combat as any other gun crew, where the mounted gunner is dismounted to fight, without considering the warhorse.

For purposes of representation, please consider a 50 mm x 100 mm base for each gun team, where all gunners (two on foot and one in warhorse) and the gun are included. Additionally Bronzino&apos;s base is 30 mm x 60 mm when he is not attached to a Galloper Gun. When he joins the unit, he is counted as part of it with same base representation.


Bronzino&apos;s Gallopers have (-1) reduced Toughness to normal cannos due to their function of mobility over form.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Galloper&apos;s Rapid Movement" id="9e16-4bc8-91ba-d71f" hidden="false" typeId="c1ac-c1c8-f9d5-9673" typeName="Special Rule">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9f84-4221-785a-db50">Each galloper gun team is harnessed to a warhorse ridden by one of the gunners of the team. This enables to move at a rapid pace like cavalry. As the warhorse movement is equivalent to the team marching, the gun may not fire if it counts as the team has marched. Galloper guns cannot march with the warhorse marching movement (16&quot;), so their movement will be always limited to (8&quot;).

When you move one of Bronzino&apos;s guns, simply measure the distance and make your move. There is no need to turn or wheel as the galloper guns can turn freely to face any direction they wish.

To represent this extraordinary mobility, galloper guns may move and fire.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Galloper Warhorse" id="7a1b-3ed5-341d-6990" hidden="false" page="Army Book of Dogs of War in Warhammer Fantasy 5th Edition" typeId="b070-143a-73f-2772" typeName="Model">
